{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew","id":1262445,"title":"The Keepers Of The World (2nd Edition Homebrew)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-23T18:19:49-07:00","id":1262445,"title":"The Keepers Of The World (2nd Edition Homebrew)","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Keepers of The World.</b></span><br /> <br /> <i>It's been centuries, millennia even. But their magnun opus is so close to done. Soon,the tyranny of the divine will be over</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">The Keepers of The World are a cross-pantheon organization that has been kept secret for thousands of years,no mean feat in this reality. Dedicated to one goal and one goal alone,the Keepers tirelessly work to achieve lt. With great strength of body and mind and a perfect plan,The goal is almost here.<br /> They are coming for the Gods,all of them.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hercules,The Greatest Greek Hero.</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Aliases:Heracles.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Hercules,son of Zeus and Alcmene. Born of sex by trickery,born of rape. The wrath of Hera followed him since he was a child,first with the attack of deadly snakes and then with awful madness. The great hero has inspired Scions for thousands of years. A lesser men would be damn near dead inside after what he went through,but he was bigger than that,better than that. His heart is still filled with righteous wrath and hot purpose.even after all these years.<br /> Twelve great Deeds plus plenty of &quot;smaller&quot; acts of heroism crowned him the Hero among Heroes, the standard all Theoi Scions must follow. Married to Hebe,a agreement made with Hera,Hercules claim to be in peace. It's a lie. How could anyone be in peace after the torment Hera inflicted upon him? His first family? dead. His second family? dead. Everyone who's ever cared for him is long dead and he won't take it anymore. Peace? It's been a long time since he realized there will never be such a thing as peace while the Theoi live. A deal was struck with the Sage Imhotep, the World will be remade and the gods will be part of it no more. Hercules shall break them like he broke so many monsters ver those years.<br /> Purviews: Epic Strenght,Epic Dexterity, Epic Stamina, Order,Fertility<br /> Callings:Hunter,Warrior,Guardian.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Imhotep,Architect of The Netjer</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Aliases:Immutef, Im-hotep,Li-em-Hotep<br /> The Architect's master plan is near completion. He can almost taste it! A World with no Gods,true freedom for one and all. That's Imhotep's dream. Once a chanceller to pharaoh Djesor,he learned the secrets of how to build wondrous monuments from his father,Ptah. Yet Imhotep has improved upon his father's designs and created many of his own. A peerlees builder,a great magician and a brilliant historian,there's very litttle imhotep can't do. Yet he's not satisfied,he saw the Kemet he loved be plagued by war,death and misery again. Petty Heru and Wesir and Sutehk,always so pre-occupied with the gathering of power disgust him. He wants the glory of old Kemet back,and if he has to destroy Egypt and the Whole World to do it,he damn well will. He's tired of seeing great monuments being erected for Gods who barely glance at them,to busy staring at their own grandeur. He has long decided humans should be the rightful rulers of the World,and they will rule it with Imhotep's guidance.<br /> Purviews:Health,Forge,Earth,Order.<br /> Callings:Sage,Creator,Guardian.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Himiko,Mother of Ojin</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Aliases:Pimiko</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">It simply ins't fair. After all she's done,she literally gave birth to freaking </span><i>hachiman. </i><span style=\"font-size:10px\">And that's the thanks she gets? This will not stand. Once a Scion of Amaterasu. Himiko grow pregnant of Emperor Ojin,incarnation of Hachiman. It took three years for the child to be born,Himiko bound herself with laces to make sure she could fight a war without being interrupted by the child. Her son,destroyed alll his enemies and brough glory to Japan. Himiko was once proud of her role in all this. But eventually the other shoe dropped. Himiko was never deified,at first she pretended it didn't bother him,but then bit by bit she wondered, Why? What sin she could have possibly made to displease her mother? The truth is,and Amaterasu didn't shy away to tell her,Himiko's Mantle was simply too weak,she just couldn't match up with her son or any of Amatsukami. She became a footnote,a curiosity. Well,when her Mother and her cronies will be forever locked in the Overworld,century upon century on a prison made of The Keepers of the World's will. They will know what is like.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u00b4Purviews:Stars,War,Order</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Calling:Warrior,Creator,Liminal.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 10-24-2018, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T18:23:09-07:00","id":1262446,"title":"","content":"this week,i'll figure out who the other members are (i'm planning on adding some new ones). And i will detail their plan <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T18:28:49-07:00","id":1262447,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty sure Heracles was worshipped as a fertility god, for whatever that is worth.<br /> <br /> Does he have Stars because of the constellation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T18:43:54-07:00","id":1262450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1262447#post1262447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure Heracles was worshipped as a fertility god, for whatever that is worth.<br /> <br /> Does he have Stars because of the constellation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah :&gt;,i feel like he's more closely connected to his constellation than the the Other Theoi are with their planets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T18:56:04-07:00","id":1262451,"title":"","content":"I think we already have the best possible Keeper recruit for the Shen: Confucius!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T19:02:52-07:00","id":1262453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1262451#post1262451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we already have the best possible Keeper recruit for the Shen: Confucius!</div> </div> </div> </div>Brilliant! He's perfect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T19:44:35-07:00","id":1262455,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> Do you know of any Member of tuatha,God,Demigod or Hero that would make a good member of the Keepers. I'm looking for someone who's have a reason to want no more gods or legendary beings or divinity in the World","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T20:00:01-07:00","id":1262456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1262455#post1262455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> Do you know of any Member of tuatha,God,Demigod or Hero that would make a good member of the Keepers. I'm looking for someone who's have a reason to want no more gods or legendary beings or divinity in the World</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, tricky call as the Pantheon's uniting goal is taking over Ireland and throwing the mortals out. They'd be pretty dead set against The Keeper's plan fundamentally.<br /> <br /> Now, Donn could be an option since Donn is just a M\u00edlisian king and not one of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann. Donn would probably be in favor of supporting his descendants in finally getting rid of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann (though his oath is to slaughter them all) but that gets into the weird territory of 'Well all the Irish mortals are sort of Legendary....'<br /> <br /> He might be a good addition to The Keepers who is going to inevitably betray the rest of them when he realizes that the plan is going against his goals and in uncertainty about how it will effect the mortals of Ireland. Also he is probably far more murderous than the rest would appreciate, his plan was to slaughter every living thing in Ireland himself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T20:15:06-07:00","id":1262458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1262456#post1262456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, tricky call as the Pantheon's uniting goal is taking over Ireland and throwing the mortals out. They'd be pretty dead set against The Keeper's plan fundamentally.<br /> <br /> Now, Donn could be an option since Donn is just a M\u00edlisian king and not one of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann. Donn would probably be in favor of supporting his descendants in finally getting rid of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann (though his oath is to slaughter them all) but that gets into the weird territory of 'Well all the Irish mortals are sort of Legendary....'<br /> <br /> He might be a good addition to The Keepers who is going to inevitably betray the rest of them when he realizes that the plan is going against his goals and in uncertainty about how it will effect the mortals of Ireland. Also he is probably far more murderous than the rest would appreciate, his plan was to slaughter every living thing in Ireland himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait,I just had an idea. I'll make one of the keepers a Scion of Donn who ascended to godhood in the seventies,and he want to banish the gods because he thinks Donn will eventually make good on his promise to destroy the people of Ireland,along with his desire to see a world of total freedom with no gods controlling people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T20:44:29-07:00","id":1262464,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sealgaire,The sword of the Dead.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Aliases:Great Hunter</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Once upon a time Donn went deep in a mountain,he found a mine full of jewels and treasure untold. He found a sword of great sharpness and beauty,using terrible magic he gave the sword life and human shape. He named the Sword Sealgaire. Sealgair went many years acting according to his origins,as a killing tool for his creator. He was sword who wielded swords ,then he moved on to move sophisticated weapons,but always he was covered in blood,a warlike monster his creator's pride. But with conscience came remorse,by the time Sealgaire ascended to godhood in 1977,he was tired of the fighting. And above all,he was tired of this creator,Donn wouldn't leave him alone,not even when he became a god. It was always &quot;kill this,devastate that&quot;, it got old. The final straw came when his creator developed a plan to convince a aggressive nation to launch a nuclear attack on Ireland,killing many innocents. Sealgaire stopped this plan,as punishment Donn buried him deep in the earth with only the cries of the Sluagh as company,he got out . But he'll never forget what he went through. Sealgaire realized the tuatha's old traditions were not only outdated,but also dangerous. their obssession with honor made them swear and stand by ridiculous oaths,his creator,even after millennia,couldn't let his vow of destruction go. Sealgaire decided the Tuatha'st ime has passed and that they must be destroyed or imprisioned for the good of the people of Ireland and the World. He met Hercules on a trip to a construction site on America,they talked about their shared woes,about their anger. Finally,Hercules revealed to the Hunter the truth about the Keepers,Sealgaire was overjoyed with the idea of freedom,a world no longer bound by such a outdated concept as &quot;Honor&quot;. And so he prepares to bury the Tuatha,just like his father wanted<br /> purviews:darkness,forge,war<br /> callings:hunter,warrior,sage</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T23:23:37-07:00","id":1262480,"title":"","content":"Nitpicking I know but Heracles doesn't do anything with Stars in mythology except being turned into one. May I suggest Order (he was the protector of several Roman Emperors)<br /> <br /> Also Guardian? I suppose it could work but Lover is a better fit IMHO, it's not part of his main myth but everything happening to him after the Twelve Trials is due to him not keeping it in his pants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T07:30:33-07:00","id":1262526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1262480#post1262480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpicking I know but Heracles doesn't do anything with Stars in mythology except being turned into one. May I suggest Order (he was the protector of several Roman Emperors)<br /> <br /> Also Guardian? I suppose it could work but Lover is a better fit IMHO, it's not part of his main myth but everything happening to him after the Twelve Trials is due to him not keeping it in his pants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh,you're right. I'll fix it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:32:01-07:00","id":1387096,"title":"","content":"Turns out!Now we have a FULL LIST OF keepers,and titles<br /> They are<br /> Imhotep, The One Who Comes in Peace <br /> Herakles, God of Strength <br /> Karna, Between Dharma and Adharma <br /> Dorje Shugden, the Enlightened Gyapo <br /> Meng Po, the Old Lady, Goddess of\u2026 <br /> Takeminakata-no-Mikoto, Prince of the Earth <br /> Tlaz\u014dlte\u014dtl, Goddess of Filth and Purification <br /> Tolui Khagan, Odchigin Youngest Son, God of Family Wayland Smith <br /> Zalmoxis, God of Blood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-09-2020, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:58:27-07:00","id":1387121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387096#post1387096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turns out!Now we have a FULL LIST OF keepers,and titles<br /> They are<br /> Imhotep, The One Who Comes in Peace Herakles, God of Strength Karna, Between Dharma and Adharma Dorje Shugden, the Enlightened Gyapo Meng Po, the Old Lady, Goddess of\u2026 Takeminakata-no-Mikoto, Prince of the Earth Tlaz\u014dlte\u014dtl, Goddess of Filth and Purification Tolui Khagan, Odchigin Youngest Son, God of Family Wayland Smith Zalmoxis, God of Blood</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be a bit hard to see where one of the Keepers ends &amp; the next begins with the list written up like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:12:56-07:00","id":1387123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387121#post1387121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can be a bit hard to see where one of the Keepers ends &amp; the next begins with the list written up like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry! Time to fix it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:22:39-07:00","id":1387128,"title":"","content":"That's an unusual list. It looks like we have a Pala, a Tanrilar, and a Thracian deity? Not what I was expecting, but certainly interesting. Does this mean the Palas are coming sooner than anticipated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:31:35-07:00","id":1387131,"title":"","content":"Let's talk about them and their motivations.<br /> Imhotep is a mystery. He's a god of buildings,an architect. Why would he want to destroy all gods? Maybe it's to build something .<br /> Karna fought on the losing side of the great war on the mahabharata epic. He was know for being incredibly honorable. Sticking to the sides of tyrants because said tyrants were kind to him. Another mystery for sure,could it be he see the death of gods as a necessity? To stop a brand new war?<br /> I've a hard time trying to figure who Doeje shugden is. He seems to be focus of a school of buddhism which wasn't accepted by other schools. Could it be he wants to be only buddhist deity to exist?<br /> Meng Po is reaponsible to wipe the memories of a soul before it's re-incarnated. After a few millennia of this,she must have seen some stufff. Perhaps she's just bitter? Or naybe she saw too many bad memories caused by the gods and can't stand it anymore.<br /> Takeminakata-no-Mikoto is a son of Okinukushi. He tried to conquer japan once and failed,this time he's probably coming with a crew at his side to make sure he suceeda.<br /> Tlaz\u014dlte\u014dtl titles says much,she wants purification. She wants cleansing. Well hell,which better way to cleanse the world thsn to wipe away all gods?<br /> Tolui Khagan and is the son a Mongolian Conqueror. Yes,that one. He had this complicated family issue, bottom line he wants nobody to be forced to do tough choices by fate ever again.<br /> Zalmoxis is a very misteryous god,he has no pantheon. Maybe he wants no pantheon but his own?<br /> Now my take is,the Keepers might dress themselves up as noble heroes. But deep down,they want revenge. That's the common thread they were wronged and they want payback.<br /> Which leads us to Heracles. No one is greek myth has a bettee motivation for revenge than he does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T17:33:06-07:00","id":1387132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387128#post1387128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an unusual list. It looks like we have a Pala, a Tanrilar, and a Thracian deity? Not what I was expecting, but certainly interesting. Does this mean the Palas are coming sooner than anticipated?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid there's not imediate books with them in the outline. I'm sorry :/<br /> Do you know anything about this Dorje Shugden fellow? He seems to be hard to find","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T19:52:15-07:00","id":1387161,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, I was unfamiliar with Dorje Shugden until looking at the list. Looking him up was the first time I'd heard of him, though I'd assume he's one of the Palas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T20:03:53-07:00","id":1387163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387096#post1387096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turns out!Now we have a FULL LIST OF keepers,and titles<br /> They are<br /> Imhotep, The One Who Comes in Peace <br /> Herakles, God of Strength <br /> Karna, Between Dharma and Adharma <br /> Dorje Shugden, the Enlightened Gyapo <br /> Meng Po, the Old Lady, Goddess of\u2026 <br /> Takeminakata-no-Mikoto, Prince of the Earth <br /> Tlaz\u014dlte\u014dtl, Goddess of Filth and Purification <br /> Tolui Khagan, Odchigin Youngest Son, God of Family<br /> Wayland Smith <br /> Zalmoxis, God of Blood</div> </div> </div> </div>We also know some of the gods who were approached but said no, including<br /> <br /> Persephone<br /> Confucius<br /> Marinette<br /> Savitr<br /> Amatsu-Mikaboshi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T20:13:26-07:00","id":1387166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387163#post1387163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We also know some of the gods who were approached but said no, including<br /> <br /> Persephone<br /> Confucius<br /> Marinette<br /> Savitr<br /> Amatsu-Mikaboshi</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, persephone probably said no out of love. Confucius is really into family relationships,maybe he felt like the gods were his family?<br /> Marinette is a lia who suffered much,i think she's just tired of fighting. Savitr is the impeller,the one sets the world in motion he probably wants it to continue in motion. I'm surprisingly Mikaboshi said no though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:40:03-07:00","id":1387225,"title":"","content":"Wait? This time the Keepers want to DESTROY all the Gods? In 1E, they just wanted to cut them off from the World. That kinda pushes them into a more villainous territory, doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:49:15-07:00","id":1387231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387225#post1387225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait? This time the Keepers want to DESTROY all the Gods? In 1E, they just wanted to cut them off from the World. That kinda pushes them into a more villainous territory, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:54:02-07:00","id":1387237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387231#post1387231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they don\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:00:47-07:00","id":1387239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387231#post1387231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they don\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I could've sworn I saw a post in here that mentioned that. Can't find it now. I guess I just jumped to conclusions with the whole &quot;They're coming for the Gods&quot; line. *Shrug.*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:18:15-07:00","id":1387242,"title":"","content":"Up in the post about the motivations of the Keepers it explicitly mentions several of them wanting to bring about the death or destruction of the gods. So yes, they do plan to kill off the gods not just cut them off from the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:26:27-07:00","id":1387246,"title":"","content":"The thing with the Keepers is that they mostly agree on a similar end result but not necessarily on the method to reach said result.<br /> Some would want the gods dead while other just want a higher degree of separation between the World and the Overworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T08:03:43-07:00","id":1387271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387242#post1387242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Up in the post about the motivations of the Keepers it explicitly mentions several of them wanting to bring about the death or destruction of the gods. So yes, they do plan to kill off the gods not just cut them off from the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are making this conclusion based on Nicholas Milioni\u2019s speculations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T08:05:19-07:00","id":1387272,"title":"","content":"I know for a fact they want to cut of the Gods. But i think thad destroy them right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T08:18:15-07:00","id":1387276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387272#post1387272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know for a fact they want to cut of the Gods. But i think thad destroy them right?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I am aware, destroying the gods as a whole is not part of the plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T08:25:16-07:00","id":1387278,"title":"","content":"Gotcha,very interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:03:46-07:00","id":1387323,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that Ushuni might make a good Keeper. He might also be too brutal and bloodthirsty even for the other Keepers to be willing to align themselves with him though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T14:24:29-07:00","id":1387329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387323#post1387323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that Ushuni might make a good Keeper. He might also be too brutal and bloodthirsty even for the other Keepers to be willing to align themselves with him though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is that??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:10:22-07:00","id":1387342,"title":"","content":"A former Hittite hybrid Scion and son of Kumarbi who became a TItan and brutally took over the pantheon in Hittite mythology. You can read about him in Watcher and Sacerdos' Shiunesh write-up. I always personally characterized him as a fallen faux-revolutionary who planned to overthrow the notoriously tyrannical Shiunesh, but whose own psychopathic nature led to him becoming a tyrant in his own right. In my &quot;headcanons,&quot; once the Shiunesh began to interact with other pantheons, his hatred expanded to all gods, even ones who weren't as brutal as his own pantheon, and has since become a feared figure throughout the World, having slain countless divinities and scions, and forming a temporary alliance with Aten, though the two planned to backstab each other as soon as they outlived their usefulness. It's entirely possible that he may be too chaotic and bloodthirsty for the Keepers to work with him, though, given that they tend to be more covert.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 05-10-2020, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:47:28-07:00","id":1387352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387132#post1387132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know anything about this Dorje Shugden fellow? He seems to be hard to find</div> </div> </div> </div>Dorje Shugden was historically a wrathful guardian deity, a protector of the Gelug school, one of the four main schools of Tibetan Buddhism--the one the Dalai Lama belongs to in fact. He's a rather sectarian deity, whose purpose is to keep Gelug monastics from converting to one of the other three schools of Tibetan Buddhism or even getting involved in Rime, a movement to promote ecumenicism within Tibetan Buddhism, specifically the idea that all four major schools are legitimate paths to enlightenment.<br /> <br /> One of the childhood tutors of the current Dalai Lama was a devotee of Dorje Shugden, but after his exile and in face of the need to build a strong Tibetan independence movement, the Dalai Lama rejected Dorje Shugden and embraced the Rime movement. Indeed, the Dalai Lama even recognized the legitimacy of Bon, which defines itself as Tibet's native, pre-Buddhist, shamanic religion. (Tibetan Buddhism, in practice, was heavily influenced by native Tibetan shamanism and Bon has absorbed many Buddhist ideas, to the point where both are arguably syncretic mixes of Tibetan shamanism and Buddhism, just with different emphases.) As a result the Dalai Lama has actively discouraged members of the Gelug school from worshiping Dorje Shugden any more, seeing him as a needlessly divisive figure.<br /> <br /> Most members of the Gelug school have gone along with this, but there is a faction that is quite angry about this and continue to worship Dorje Shugden, verbally attacking the Dalai Lama, accusing him of promoting their oppression. (Amnesty International has concluded that, while Dorje Shugden worshipers do face some stigma in the Tibetan exile community, they are not being oppressed or politically prosecuted by the Dalai Lama's government in exile.) The Chinese government has tried to take advantage of the divisions and has supported Dorje Shudgen worshipers in occupied Tibet. There's even a break-away sect, the New Kadampa Traditions, devoted entirely to Dorje Shugden and his earthly representative Kelsang Gyatso. They're based in Britain, where they have most of their followers, but can be found throughout the West.<br /> <br /> Tricycle, a major Western Buddhist magazine, has a good article on the whole thing <a href=\"https://tricycle.org/magazine/the-one-pure-dharma/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. I think you can access it for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T15:52:20-07:00","id":1387354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muskrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387352#post1387352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dorje Shugden was historically a wrathful guardian deity, a protector of the Gelug school, one of the four main schools of Tibetan Buddhism--the one the Dalai Lama belongs to in fact. He's a rather sectarian deity, whose purpose is to keep Gelug monastics from converting to one of the other three schools of Tibetan Buddhism or even getting involved in Rime, a movement to promote ecumenicism within Tibetan Buddhism, specifically the idea that all four major schools are legitimate paths to enlightenment.<br /> <br /> One of the childhood tutors of the current Dalai Lama was a devotee of Dorje Shugden, but after his exile and in face of the need to build a strong Tibetan independence movement, the Dalai Lama rejected Dorje Shugden and embraced the Rime movement. Indeed, the Dalai Lama even recognized the legitimacy of Bon, which defines itself as Tibet's native, pre-Buddhist, shamanic religion. (Tibetan Buddhism, in practice, was heavily influenced by native Tibetan shamanism and Bon has absorbed many Buddhist ideas, to the point where both are arguably syncretic mixes of Tibetan shamanism and Buddhism, just with different emphases.) As a result the Dalai Lama has actively discouraged members of the Gelug school from worshiping Dorje Shugden any more, seeing him as a needlessly divisive figure.<br /> <br /> Most members of the Gelug school have gone along with this, but there is a faction that is quite angry about this and continue to worship Dorje Shugden, verbally attacking the Dalai Lama, accusing him of promoting their oppression. (Amnesty International has concluded that, while Dorje Shugden worshipers do face some stigma in the Tibetan exile community, they are not being oppressed or politically prosecuted by the Dalai Lama's government in exile.) The Chinese government has tried to take advantage of the divisions and has supported Dorje Shudgen worshipers in occupied Tibet. There's even a break-away sect, the New Kadampa Traditions, devoted entirely to Dorje Shugden and his earthly representative Kelsang Gyatso. They're based in Britain, where they have most of their followers, but can be found throughout the West.<br /> <br /> Tricycle, a major Western Buddhist magazine, has a good article on the whole thing <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://tricycle.org/magazine/the-one-pure-dharma/&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. I think you can access it for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very interesting. I can see why Dorje Shugden might wanna banish the competition<br /> Do you know what his title,Enlightened Gyapo,means? Is a Gyapo a kind of monk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T16:15:10-07:00","id":1387357,"title":"","content":"Very Cool, Nicolas Miloni. I have just started my campaign and decided to make the Keepers the big bads of my campaign. I also put Karna in the Keepers, but he's a reincarnated Hero at the moment, not a God.<br /> I'm a huge fan of the Mahabharata after i read it for Exalted inspiration and Karna is my favourite character in it. My list is different from yours, but i think i will use yours with your permission?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T16:29:02-07:00","id":1387360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387357#post1387357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very Cool, Nicolas Miloni. I have just started my campaign and decided to make the Keepers the big bads of my campaign. I also put Karna in the Keepers, but he's a reincarnated Hero at the moment, not a God.<br /> I'm a huge fan of the Mahabharata after i read it for Exalted inspiration and Karna is my favourite character in it. My list is different from yours, but i think i will use yours with your permission?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi! Im so sorry. But the list isn't mine. It's from the Scion team. I'm sure they'll let you use it though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T16:56:40-07:00","id":1387361,"title":"","content":"To clarify some apparent confusion going on. The lineup of the members we have and those who were offered but said no, are from the writers on the Scion Discord. All the commentary about motives has been fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T17:09:30-07:00","id":1387364,"title":"","content":"precisely that yes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T19:22:14-07:00","id":1387394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1262445-the-keepers-of-the-world-2nd-edition-homebrew?p=1387354#post1387354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's very interesting. I can see why Dorje Shugden might wanna banish the competition<br /> Do you know what his title,Enlightened Gyapo,means? Is a Gyapo a kind of monk?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;gyalpo&quot; refers to a protective deity. I think part of the debate revolving around him is whether is actually enlightened or not. His most devout followers, such as the New Kadampa Tradition, see him as enlightened, but I don't think that view is widely held, even among members of the Gelug school--and certainly not outside it.<br /> <br /> So Dorje Shugden might consider himself enlightened and be resentful that other Buddhist deities don't recognize him as such. Which would parallel plenty of real world disputes among human Buddhist teachers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}